.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt MPORT.CREATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mport.create
.Nd create an mport package bundle from package metadata and a plist
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl n Ar name
.Fl v Ar version
.Fl o Ar output-file
.Fl s Ar source-dir
.Fl p Ar plist-file
.Fl P Ar prefix
.Fl O Ar origin
.Fl t Ar categories
.Op Fl c Ar comment
.Op Fl f Ar flavor
.Op Fl e Ar cpe
.Op Fl l Ar language
.Op Fl D Ar depends
.Op Fl C Ar conflicts
.Op Fl A Ar annotations
.Op Fl d Ar pkg-descr
.Op Fl i Ar pkg-install
.Op Fl j Ar pkg-deinstall
.Op Fl m Ar pkg-message
.Op Fl M Ar mtree
.Op Fl E Ar expiration-date
.Op Fl S Ar no-provide-shlib
.Op Fl L Ar lua-script-dir
.Op Fl x Ar deprecated-message
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates a
.Pa .mport
package bundle using metadata supplied on the command line, a plist file, and
a source directory containing the packaged files.
It is primarily a packaging helper used during package build workflows.
.Pp
The following arguments are required:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl O Ar origin"
.It Fl n Ar name
Package name.
.It Fl v Ar version
Package version.
.It Fl o Ar output-file
Output package filename.
.It Fl s Ar source-dir
Directory containing the packaged files, typically the fake destdir.
.It Fl p Ar plist-file
Packing list file to parse.
.It Fl P Ar prefix
Installation prefix recorded in the package metadata.
.It Fl O Ar origin
Package origin, such as
.Dq editors/vim .
.It Fl t Ar categories
Comma-separated category list.
.El
.Pp
The following optional arguments are supported:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl x Ar deprecated-message"
.It Fl c Ar comment
Short package comment.
.It Fl f Ar flavor
Package flavor.
.It Fl e Ar cpe
Package CPE identifier.
.It Fl l Ar language
Package language metadata.
.It Fl D Ar depends
Comma-separated dependency list.
.It Fl C Ar conflicts
Comma-separated conflict list.
.It Fl A Ar annotations
Comma-separated annotation list.
.It Fl d Ar pkg-descr
Path to the package description file.
.It Fl i Ar pkg-install
Path to the package install script.
.It Fl j Ar pkg-deinstall
Path to the package deinstall script.
.It Fl m Ar pkg-message
Path to the package message file.
.It Fl M Ar mtree
Path to the mtree file.
.It Fl E Ar expiration-date
Expiration date in
.Dq YYYY-MM-DD
format.
.It Fl S Ar no-provide-shlib
Record that the package provides no shared libraries to other packages,
even if it ships some, for example a port that bundles private copies.
Truthy values include
.Dq 1 ,
.Dq y ,
and
.Dq t .
Without this option the record follows the shared library scan described
under
.Sx SHARED LIBRARIES .
.Xr mport 1
uses the record to accept such a package as a dependency even when it was
built for an earlier MidnightBSD release.
.It Fl L Ar lua-script-dir
Directory containing the Lua hook scripts
.Pa pkg-pre-install.lua ,
.Pa pkg-post-install.lua ,
.Pa pkg-pre-deinstall.lua ,
and
.Pa pkg-post-deinstall.lua .
Each script runs with these globals set:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va pkg_shlibs_provided" -compact
.It Va pkg_name
The package name.
.It Va pkg_prefix
The installation prefix.
.It Va pkg_rootdir
The root the package is installed under.
.It Va pkg_upgrade
True when the package replaces an installed version.
.It Va pkg_shlibs_provided
Array of the shared library sonames the package provides; see
.Sx SHARED LIBRARIES .
.It Va pkg_shlibs_required
Array of the sonames it requires from other packages.
.El
Both arrays are empty for a package built before shared libraries were
recorded.
.It Fl x Ar deprecated-message
Deprecation message to record in the package metadata.
.El
.Sh SHARED LIBRARIES
Every regular file in the package is read as an ELF object.
An object carrying a
.Dv DT_SONAME
provides that library and every
.Dv DT_NEEDED
entry names a library the package requires.
Only names beginning with
.Dq lib
are considered.
The lists are stored in the package as
.Cm shlibs_provided
and
.Cm shlibs_required ,
and the package is marked as providing no shared libraries when the
provided list is empty.
.Pp
Objects for another word size or operating system are tracked with a
suffix, as
.Xr pkg 8
does on FreeBSD:
.Dq libfoo.so.1:32
for a 32-bit object on a 64-bit target,
.Dq libfoo.so.1:Linux
for a Linux object and
.Dq libfoo.so.1:Linux:32
for both.
.Pp
A library the package requires is dropped from the required list when the
package itself installs it, under any path, since nothing else is needed to
satisfy it.
A symbolic link is read through its target only when the target lies inside
the staged tree; a link that points outside it, or at nothing, is ignored
rather than resolved against the build host.
A package whose shared objects carry no soname, or whose libraries are all
outside the provide paths, is recorded as providing none.
.Pp
The following environment variables shape the lists.
Each holds a comma separated list, so a pattern cannot itself contain a
comma, and a regular expression that does not compile stops the package
from being created.
The ports collection sets them from
.Va USE_LDCONFIG ,
.Va LIB_DIRS ,
.Va NO_SHLIB_REQUIRES_GLOB
and
.Va NO_SHLIBS_REQUIRES_REGEX .
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_COMPAT_LINUX_32"
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_NATIVE
Directories whose native libraries the package provides to others.
A library installed anywhere else is private to the package: it is left
out of the provided list but still cancels the package's own requirement
for it.
When unset, every library is provided.
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_COMPAT_32
The same for 32-bit objects on a 64-bit target.
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_COMPAT_LINUX
The same for Linux objects.
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_COMPAT_LINUX_32
The same for 32-bit Linux objects.
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_IGNORE_GLOB
.Xr fnmatch 3
patterns; a provided library matching one is dropped.
.It Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_IGNORE_REGEX
Extended regular expressions with the same effect.
.It Ev SHLIB_REQUIRE_IGNORE_GLOB
Patterns; a required library matching one is dropped.
.It Ev SHLIB_REQUIRE_IGNORE_REGEX
Extended regular expressions with the same effect.
.El
.Pp
The plist keyword
.Cm @ldconfig
and the provided list are expected to agree.
A warning is printed when the keyword is present but no native shared
library was found under
.Ev SHLIB_PROVIDE_PATHS_NATIVE ,
and when native shared libraries are provided but the plist has no
.Cm @ldconfig ,
since the run-time linker will not find them until ldconfig runs.
Neither stops the package from being created.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev ABI_FILE"
.It Ev ABI_FILE
Path to a binary built for the target system, for cross builds and jails
where it differs from the build host.
The ports collection sets it to
.Pa ${CROSS_SYSROOT}/bin/sh
when
.Va CROSS_SYSROOT
is set.
The MidnightBSD ABI note in that file gives the release recorded in the
package, ahead of the
.Cm target_os
setting and the running system, and the file's word size is the target's
when the shared library scan decides which objects are 32-bit compat
objects; a 64-bit object in a package for a 32-bit target is not
scanned.
A file without a MidnightBSD ABI note sets only the word size.
A file that cannot be read or is not an ELF object stops the package from
being created rather than recording the build host's release.
.El
.Pp
The shared library scan also reads the variables listed under
.Sx SHARED LIBRARIES .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a package bundle from a fake destdir:
.Dl $ mport.create -n hello -v 1.0 -o hello-1.0.mport -s work/stage -p pkg-plist -P /usr/local -O misc/hello -t misc
.Pp
Create a package with scripts and package message metadata:
.Dl $ mport.create -n hello -v 1.0 -o hello-1.0.mport -s work/stage -p pkg-plist -P /usr/local -O misc/hello -t misc -i pkg-install -j pkg-deinstall -m pkg-message
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mport 1 ,
.Xr mport.install 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Mx 0.3 .
